// One row per Heartbeat record - the agent's periodic "I am alive" ping, the ground truth for
// which VMs are monitored and when each was last seen. Raw grain: the agent beats about once a
// minute, so this runs to hundreds of rows per VM per hour.
//
// Loaded by Search-MsecLogAnalytics -Subject VM -Name Heartbeat -WorkspaceName <ws>.
// For a per-VM roster (last-seen and signal counts, one row per machine) use -Name All instead,
// which folds these beats down server-side and survives a much wider -Days.
//
// A single-table query on purpose: unlike -Name All this does NOT use isfuzzy, so a workspace
// with no Heartbeat table errors naming the missing table rather than returning blank. That is
// the honest answer to "show me heartbeats" from a workspace that collects none.
//
// NO TIME FILTER IN THIS FILE - Search-MsecLogAnalytics passes -Days to the API as a server-side
// timespan. VOLUME: at ~1 beat/minute/VM, a wide -Days here is large; prefer -Name All for a
// standing roster and reserve this for confirming a specific VM's beat cadence over a short
// window.

Heartbeat
| project TimeGenerated,
          Computer,
          OSType         = tostring(OSType),
          OSName         = tostring(column_ifexists('OSName', '')),
          OSMajorVersion = tostring(column_ifexists('OSMajorVersion', '')),
          AgentVersion   = tostring(column_ifexists('Version', '')),
          Category       = tostring(column_ifexists('Category', '')),
          ComputerIP     = tostring(column_ifexists('ComputerIP', '')),
          RemoteIPCountry = tostring(column_ifexists('RemoteIPCountry', '')),
          ResourceId     = tolower(tostring(column_ifexists('_ResourceId', '')))
| order by TimeGenerated desc
